{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. You're here for your 21st cycle of high-dose methotrexate. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, I'm okay. A little nervous, but I know the routine by now. I just hope I don’t get those headaches again like last time with Zofran."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We remember that. This time, we’re giving fosaprepitant and dexamethasone instead to prevent nausea — no Zofran — so you should avoid the headaches."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, good. That’s a relief. When will the chemo start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start the methotrexate infusion tonight at 6 PM. We’ll keep your urine alkalized with IV bicarbonate to protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, I’ve had trouble with the bicarb pills before — they make me nauseous. I’m glad we’re doing it through the IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:08:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We want to make this as smooth as possible. We’ll also start leucovorin 24 hours after the chemo to help clear the methotrexate safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my other meds — like gabapentin and citalopram — will I keep taking those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:11:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll continue both. We’ve paused your mesalamine for your colitis during the stay, but we’ll restart it when you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:12:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my aspirin? I know I stopped the blood thinner a while back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:13:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on heparin shots while you’re here for clot prevention. We hold the aspirin during chemo, but you’ll restart it at discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I just worry about the clots, with my history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-08-30 11:16:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We do too, which is why we’re using heparin. You’re in good hands."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-08-30 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting the methotrexate now. It’ll take a few hours. Let us know if you feel any discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-08-30 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ll let you know if anything feels off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-08-31 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How did you sleep? Any nausea or headaches overnight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-08-31 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not great. I had some nausea and couldn’t sleep — my mind was racing. I took the Ativan and Compazine you left for me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-08-31 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry you had a rough night. The fosaprepitant usually helps, but sometimes chemo can still cause these side effects. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-08-31 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that normal? The racing thoughts?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-08-31 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s not common, but some patients report mood changes or restlessness. It could be from the chemo or the medications. We’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-08-31 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m feeling calmer now. Just tired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-08-31 07:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. Your labs this morning look stable — no signs of kidney or liver issues. Your blood counts are holding up well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-08-31 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the methotrexate level?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-08-31 07:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check it again today and tomorrow. So far, it’s clearing as expected. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-08-31 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to do a brain MRI today — part of your routine surveillance to check for any changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-08-31 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that scheduled for today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-08-31 13:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, in about an hour. It’s just to make sure there’s no recurrence. Your last one was clear, so we’re hopeful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-08-31 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope so. I’ve been feeling okay neurologically — no weakness or dizziness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-08-31 13:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. Your strength and coordination still look good on exam."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — the MRI results are back. No new lesions, no enhancement. Just stable chronic changes from before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s such a relief. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, excellent. Your methotrexate level this morning is 0.18 micromolar — that’s low enough to be safe. We can plan for discharge today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s great. What about the leucovorin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take a short course of oral leucovorin at home — same as last time. It’ll help finish clearing the chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds — everything goes back to normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Restart your mesalamine, gabapentin, citalopram, and aspirin. Use your inhalers as usual. We’ll send a list with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I feel nauseous again at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use the prochlorperazine or lorazepam as needed. Call us if it’s severe or lasts more than a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-09-01 09:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see Dr. ___ in two weeks for your next oncology check. We’ll also review your blood work then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-09-01 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. Your discharge orders are ready. You’re doing well — keep up with your meds and rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-09-01 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I really appreciate the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-09-01 15:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you soon in clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-09-01 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Have a good day."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-08-30 10:45:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-09-01 16:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma was admitted for her 21st cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She experienced mild nausea and insomnia with racing thoughts during the first night but remained otherwise stable. Methotrexate was administered safely with IV bicarbonate for urine alkalinization and fosaprepitant for nausea prophylaxis, avoiding Zofran due to prior headaches. Leucovorin rescue was initiated 24 hours post-infusion. Methotrexate levels declined appropriately, reaching 0.18 micromolar by discharge. A surveillance brain MRI showed no new or enhancing lesions, with only stable chronic changes. She remained neurologically intact, and her chronic conditions, including depression, asthma, ulcerative colitis, and right leg pain, were managed without complication. Aspirin was held during admission with heparin bridging for DVT prophylaxis and was restarted at discharge. She was discharged home in stable condition with a short course of oral leucovorin and instructions to resume her baseline medications.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Ulcerative colitis, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Pain in limb",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Tarsal tunnel syndrome",
      "Personal history of pulmonary embolism",
      "Antineoplastic chemotherapy induced anemia",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Nausea alone",
      "Headache",
      "Unspecified hereditary and idiopathic peripheral neuropathy"
    ]
  }
}
